# What this repo generates, and nothing else.
#
# `recurse.yaml` is deliberately *not* ignored. It holds no secrets — it is the one
# place every number that shapes the game is written down, and the builder refuses
# to run without it, so a clone that arrived without it could not rebuild the data.
#
# `server/.env` is the opposite on all three counts: it names a database, a port and
# an origin allowlist, all of which differ per deployment. `server/.env.example` is
# what is committed. See server/README.md.

node_modules/
dist/
dist-e2e/

# Rust builder
tools/graphgen/target/
# Playwright: the report and the trace/video scratch dir. The screenshots in
playwright-report/
e2e/.results/
e2e/shots/

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Logs and caches
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm

# The live progress line a long build publishes for the status line to read. Deleted
# when the build finishes; present only while one is running.
.claude-progress


# The cached search result, keyed on everything the search depends on. See bank.rs.
tools/cache/
tools/cache/bank-*.tsv

public/data/

# The optional server: its configuration, and the only copy of everybody's history.
# `node_modules/` and `dist/` above already cover its build.
server/.env
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# The client's own build-time settings, which is only ever `VITE_RECURSE_API` —
# where the optional server is, if there is one. Absent means there is none, which
# is what a downloaded copy of the game should be.
.env
.env.local
